{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception interface, with open-loop motion pulses and discrete obstacle sensor events. The specification enforces safe exploration with a strong bias toward forward progress, always turning right (rotate_clockwise) for any obstacle, and only allowing move_forward when the path is clear. All obstacle events force a transition to a recovery state where only rotate_clockwise is enabled. After recovery, the robot waits for path_clear before resuming forward motion. No state enables both move_forward and rotate_clockwise, and all transitions are deterministic.",
  "strategy": [
    "Model robot motion and perception as a single plant automaton with explicit commit states for each controllable action.",
    "Specification automaton enforces: (1) move_forward only when clear, (2) rotate_clockwise as the only recovery/turn action, (3) immediate recovery on any obstacle event, (4) return to forward progress as soon as path_clear is observed."
